    <exercise number="295" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] The position of a moving hockey puck after $$t$$ seconds is $$s(t) = \tan^{-1}t$$ where $$s$$ is in meters.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Find the velocity of the hockey puck at any time $$t.$$</item>
          <item>Find the acceleration of the puck at any time $$t.$$</item>
          <item>Evaluate a. and b. for $$t = 2,4,$$ and $$6$$ seconds.</item>
          <item>What conclusion can be drawn from the results in c.?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>a. $$v(t)=11+t2v(t)=11+t2$$ b. $$a(t)=-2t(1+t2)2a(t)=-2t(1+t2)2$$ c. $$(a)0.2,0.06,0.03;(b)-0.16,-0.028,-0.0088(a)0.2,0.06,0.03;(b)-0.16,-0.028,-0.0088$$ d. The hockey puck is decelerating/slowing down at 2, 4, and 6 seconds.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
