    <exercise number="297" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] A pole stands 75 feet tall. An angle $$\theta$$ is formed when wires of various lengths of $$x$$ feet are attached from the ground to the top of the pole, as shown in the following figure. Find the rate of change of the angle $$\frac{d\theta}{dx}$$ when a wire of length 90 feet is attached.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$-0.0168-0.0168$$ radians per foot</paragraph>
      </solution>
